            #ConstraintsOnBracketInSuperLieAlgebraInducedByVectorSpace.num_remark
              %h6#remark Remark
              %p
                By
                %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:SuperLieBracketOnDegree0InSuperLieAlgebraInducedFromVectorSpace"} (2)
                the definition
                %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:SuperLieBracketInSuperLieAlgebraInducedFromVectorSpace"} (3)
                is equivalent to
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi f
                      %mo ,
                      %mi g
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo ,
                      %mi v
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo =
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi f
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi g
                      %mo ,
                      %mi v
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mrow
                          %mi deg
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mi deg
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi g
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi g
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi f
                      %mo ,
                      %mi v
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      [ [f,g],v ]
                      \\;=\;
                      [f, [g,v] ]
                      \-
                      (-1)^{
                      deg(f) deg(g)
                      }
                      [ g, [f,v] ]
              %p
                Hence
                %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:SuperLieBracketInSuperLieAlgebraInducedFromVectorSpace"} (3)
                is already implied by
                %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:SuperLieBracketOnDegree0InSuperLieAlgebraInducedFromVectorSpace"} (2)
                if the bracket is to satisfy the
                %a{:href => "super+Lie+algebra#eq:GradedJacobiIdentity"} super Jacobi identity
            %p It remains to show that:
            #SuperJacobiForSuperLieAlgebraInducedFromVectorSpace.num_prop
              %h6#proposition Proposition
              %p
                Def.
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TheSuperLieAlgebraInducedFromVectorSpace"}
                indeed gives a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Lie+algebra"} super Lie algebra
                in that the bracket
                %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:SuperLieBracketInSuperLieAlgebraInducedFromVectorSpace"} (3)
                satisfies the
                = succeed "." do
                  %a{:href => "super+Lie+algebra#eq:GradedJacobiIdentity"} super Jacobi identity
            .proof
              %h6#proof Proof
              %p
                We proceed by
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/induction"} induction
              %p
                By Remark
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ConstraintsOnBracketInSuperLieAlgebraInducedByVectorSpace"}
                we have that the super Jacobi identity holds for all
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/triples"} triples
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
